BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 594.0 Tm (Discussion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 574.0 Tm (A brief gratitude exercise raised life satisfaction relative to a neutral listing task, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 560.0 Tm (an effect of medium size. Because the control task matched the gratitude task in time and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 546.0 Tm (structure, the difference is unlikely to reflect demand to write or reflect each evening.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 532.0 Tm (These findings support recommending brief gratitude journaling to students who wish to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 518.0 Tm (improve their well-being.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 496.0 Tm (Limitations include the student sample, the short follow-up and reliance on self-report.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 482.0 Tm (Future work should test whether the effect persists beyond the end of the intervention and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 468.0 Tm (whether it generalises to community samples.) Tj ET
